{"name":"Baby Spinach","hex":"#89a882","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.\n\nA very young human, even if not yet born.","A very young human, even if not yet born."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"spinach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any member of species Spinacia oleracea of edible plants, or its leaves.","Any of numerous plants, or their leaves, which are used for greens in the same way Spinacia oleracea is or resemble it in some way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spinach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spinach","blocks":[{"text":"Spinach is a leafy green flowering plant native to Central and Western Asia. It is of the order Caryophyllales, family Amaranthaceae, subfamily Chenopodioideae. Its leaves are a common vegetable consumed either fresh, cooked or after storage. The taste differs considerably between cooked and raw: the high oxalate content may be reduced by blanching."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_Spinazie_bloeiend.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spinach"},{"title":"Infant","blocks":[{"text":"An infant is a very young human being. Baby is an alternative term for infant. The terms may also be used to refer to juvenile beings of other organisms. A newborn is, in mainstream use, an infant who is only hours, days, or weeks old; while in medical contexts, a newborn or neonate is an infant in the first 28 days after birth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg/330px-The_newborn_baby_in_men.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infant"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg/500px-Illustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustration_Spinacia_oleracea1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/250px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/330px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg/250px-Spinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpinacia_oleracea_male_flowers%2C_spinazie_mannelijke_bloemen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Spinacia_oleracea_female_flowers%2C_spinazie_vrouwel